From 69bec987fb0e4a5aa605b53b3b1db1a71220f2ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Vagin <avagin@openvz.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Apr 2018 16:31:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fs: add SUSFS v2.0.0 support with required backports and
 fixes

Integrate SUSFS v2.0.0 with manual hooks and required compatibility
backports for 4.14 kernels.

Core changes:
- Add SUSFS implementation (mount hiding, sucompat)
- Remove inline hooks; use manual hook model for non-GKI kernels
- Restore try_umount support and align behavior with upstream 5.10

Backports and dependencies:
- IDA/IDR API updates and namespace conversions
- procfs/smaps optimizations and refactors
- pkeys stubs and related mm updates

Behavior and reliability improvements:
- Fix persistence issues by using inode->i_state for AS_FLAGS_
- Rework mount ID/group handling to avoid collisions and gaps
- Switch to fsnotify-based monitoring for /data/media/0 (event-driven)
- Defer fsnotify cleanup to avoid SRCU self-deadlock
- Refine sucompat timing based on /sdcard/Android/data availability
- Persistently track SUS mounts for KSU domains

Cleanups and adjustments:
- Rename APIs for clarity (non-su process handling)
- Remove unused code and deprecated auto features
- Adjust default mount ID ranges to avoid OEM conflicts

These changes bring SUSFS closer to upstream behavior while ensuring
stability and compatibility on non-GKI Android kernels.

